gpu-unlock (3.0.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Merge the upstream 3.0.0-beta line: CMP 170HX compute, PCIe Gen2, BAR1 and
    peer-to-peer support, ECC and VBIOS registry overrides delivered before the
    driver binds, GDDR and HBM temperatures over hwmon, an HBM clock governor
    and the GA100 and A100 power and core-clock ranges, unlocks restored at
    device resume, and release snapshots and DKMS sources restricted to an
    explicit file list.
  * The module source is no longer suffixed by the pinned driver version: the
    per-version files are unlock.c, firmware.c, layout.c, prep.c and vbios.c,
    and the transaction is split across host, memory, vram, vpr, fuses,
    inforom, overrides, pcie, pm and hbm.
  * Load gpu_unlock ahead of nvidia with a modprobe softdep in every
    initramfs, which replaces the load-order drop-in naming and the
    init-premount script.

 -- Zagitta <zetlon+github@gmail.com>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

gpu-unlock (2.5.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Carry the laptop SKUs the field measured, each one line in the card table
    and on its family's existing assets. The success reports gave TU106BM
    0x1f50, GA107 0x25a2, 0x25ac, 0x25ad and 0x25ed, AD103M 0x2717, AD104M
    0x27e0 and AD107M 0x28a1; the pre-boot project's device matrix logged
    TU104M 0x1e93, TU104BM 0x1ed1, TU106M 0x1f14 and 0x1f15 and GA107BM
    0x25e2 unlocked with the chip id our table already carries for that die.
    Every one of them is pinned, with its chip, in the host test.

 -- Zagitta <zetlon+github@gmail.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

gpu-unlock (2.4.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Prepare the Booter and the Falcon loader of every selected card, not of
    every firmware bundle: a bundle is keyed by the firmware description, and
    a family can share one, so TU116 next to a TU104 card in the same round
    got the TU102 assets and no Booter image of its own.
  * Derive the TU116 Booter image, its payload and the TU116 family from the
    TU116 bindata of the pinned driver: extract booter_load_tu116.bin,
    MODULE_FIRMWARE() it, and pin its geometry in the host test. The die
    gets no id in the card table: with the TU10x image its Booter stalls in
    the nonsecure stub, and with its own the whole transaction completes and
    the stock driver then refuses the card ("unexpected WPR2 already up,
    cannot proceed with booting GSP"), so the material is present and the
    card is not, as for GA100.
  * Make the TrueNAS kernel-headers gate assert with a test that exits
    non-zero itself; a pipeline beginning with ! is exempt from errexit, so
    the check there could never fail the job.
  * Drop the apostrophes from the AUR publish prompts. Bash parsed them as
    quotes inside the ${VAR:?...} defaults and left the publish script
    unparseable.

 -- Zagitta <zetlon+github@gmail.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

gpu-unlock (2.3.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Add a packager-free build and install path: make install-local builds
    the module through DKMS and places its firmware, the licenses and the
    initramfs drop-ins by hand, for distros with no native packager.
  * Add TrueNAS SCALE support: a prebuilt module bundle with an on-box
    firmware generator, a Guix System port with a native module package and
    a boot-time shepherd one-shot, an install script for rpm-ostree
    systems, a reusable Nix flake with an opt-in NixOS module, and
    openSUSE packaging.
  * Contain a late unlock failure with the success path's FLR, so a Booter
    that halts after the privileged writes leaves the card reset and
    re-unlockable at the next boot instead of held until power off.
  * Accept the NvU64-word bindata codegen, so the boot assets extract from
    the newer NVIDIA source trees.
  * Name the modules to dracut when rebuilding on install, so the module
    lands in the image on deb and rpm installs.

 -- Zagitta <zetlon+github@gmail.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

gpu-unlock (2.2.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Unlock Turing (TU102, TU104 and TU106) with the two-write chain: the
    Booter opens WPR_CFG_PLM and then the FEAT aperture, and the GSP launch
    tolerates a halted engine before the FWSEC v2 loader, settles after the
    GSP reset and polls the TU10x scrub in DMACTL. TU116 and TU117 (the GTX
    16 series) stay out of the table: their Booter image is not derived yet.
  * Add the GA103M RTX 3080 Ti Laptop id.
  * Document unlocking for virtualized GPUs.
  * Run the host unit tests of the parsers and the recipe table in CI, and
    assert all three initramfs-tools drop-ins in the package round-trip.

 -- Zagitta <zetlon+github@gmail.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

gpu-unlock (2.1.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Add GA107 and the reported GA106 and AD106 laptop SKUs.
  * Pad Booter DMEM sizes to the Falcon DMA granularity.
  * Build on kernels older than 5.16, which have no pci_dev_lock().
  * Rebuild dracut initramfs images when installing the deb package, and
    load gpu_unlock ahead of nvidia by naming the dracut drop-in
    00-gpu-unlock.conf.
  * Add tools/bench_gemm.c.

